// Used when: A contributor or catalogue inspection needs the generated list of rail assembly blueprints, picture and manual-record paths, placement/type counts, and recorded coverage summaries.
// Read by: Human readers and catalogue regression checks; it accompanies 01_assemblies/INVENTORY.md as generated data. Assembly menu preparation and connection analysis read registered assembly.json plans and subject records rather than this summary.
// Updated by: scp.inventory.write_inventories, called by python3 -B custom-pieces/scp.py inventory and the full documentation refresh, reads saved placement plans, connections.json, image availability, and checks/manual-tests.json. Edit those owning records and regenerate.
// Affects: The browseable assembly index, coverage totals, and connection-matrix summaries. Placements and game observations remain owned by each assembly; generating this index neither creates a one-click assembly nor confirms that its traffic works.
// Reference: custom-pieces/docs/WORKFLOW_DOCUMENTATION_GENERATION.md#9-maintain-the-complete-preview-catalogue.
